# Production build values, committed deliberately.
#
# Vite substitutes VITE_* at BUILD time, not runtime. The first Cloudflare
# deploy set these as Worker runtime variables instead, so `vite build` never
# saw them: the bundle shipped with no URL at all and `lib/supabase.ts` refused
# to start — a green build and a dead app.
#
# Committing them removes the whole class of failure. The build is now
# reproducible anywhere — CI, Cloudflare, a fresh clone — with no dashboard
# state to get wrong, and these are the same two values already visible in
# every shipped bundle. `.env.example` says it plainly: both are public by
# design.
#
# The SERVICE ROLE / sb_secret_ key is NOT among them and must never appear
# here — it bypasses every policy in supabase/migrations, including the two
# that close the forged-verification and forged-match defects.
#
# `npm run dev` runs in development mode and does not read this file, so
# .env.local still decides what your dev server talks to.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://kgfxzjgpjsiaxvlneufz.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable__zs_Raa-O507VH0cFkyLfQ_FUiwNL7T
